## Where to look

| To | Look in |
|---|---|
{{#if (eq language "java")}}
| add an endpoint, or change who may call it | `backend/src/main/java/{{project.packagePath}}/note/api/` |
| change what happens when a note is saved | `note/application/NoteService.java` |
| add a feature | a new folder beside `note/`, with the same four (`api`, `application`, `domain`, `infrastructure`) |
| add a permission | `common/config/Setup.java` |
| add a column or a table | a new file in `backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/` |
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq language "node")}}
| add an endpoint, or change who may call it | `backend/src/note/routes.ts` |
| add a feature | a new folder beside `src/note/`, wired into `src/app.ts` |
| add a permission | `backend/src/common/setup.ts` |
| add a column or a table | a new file in `backend/migrations/`, then `prisma/schema.prisma` and `npx prisma generate` |
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq language "python")}}
| add an endpoint, or change who may call it | `backend/src/{{project.module}}/note/routes.py` |
| add a feature | a new folder beside `note/`, wired into `app.py` |
| add a permission | `backend/src/{{project.module}}/common/seeding.py` |
| add a column or a table | a new file in `backend/migrations/` |
{{/if}}
{{#if cap.email}}
| change an email | `{{#if (eq language "java")}}backend/src/main/resources/notification-templates/{{else}}backend/notification-templates/{{/if}}` (`email.subject.txt`, `email.body.html`) |
{{/if}}
| change a setting | `backend/.env.example` lists them; set them in the environment |
{{#if frontend}}
| add a page | `frontend/src/modules/<feature>/`{{#if (eq frontend "vite")}}, and a route in `frontend/src/app/App.tsx`{{else}}, and a route in `frontend/src/app/`{{/if}} |
{{/if}}

## Run it

1. **Access to the SDK's packages.** They are on GitHub Packages, which asks for a token even to read. Create a token
   (classic) with the scope `read:packages` and keep it in `GITHUB_TOKEN`. `backend/README.md` says how{{#if (eq language "java")}} Maven{{/if}}{{#if (eq language "node")}} npm{{/if}}{{#if (eq language "python")}} uv{{/if}} reads it.
{{#if extra.compose}}
2. **The services:** `docker compose up -d`, from this folder.
{{else}}
2. **A database:** PostgreSQL with a database named `{{project.module}}` (user `postgres`, password `postgres` by default).
{{/if}}
3. **The backend:** see `backend/README.md`. It answers on http://localhost:8080.
{{#if frontend}}
4. **The frontend:** see `frontend/README.md`. It runs on {{#if (eq frontend "vite")}}http://localhost:5173{{else}}http://localhost:3000{{/if}}.
{{/if}}

On the first start the SDK creates its tables, then this application's, generates its signing keys in `backend/keys`,
and creates the platform's administrator. The application then adds its permissions (`note.read`, `note.write`) and a
demo organization, *Demo*, whose administrator is **ada@example.com** / **demo-password**.
{{#if cap.email}}

The email to a note's author is in Mailpit: <http://localhost:8025>.
{{/if}}
{{#if cap.tracing}}

Traces are in Jaeger (<http://localhost:16686>), metrics in Prometheus (<http://localhost:9090>).
{{/if}}

Learn more on the EGRADX Developer Portal: guides for each capability, recipes, and the reference.
